IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa3-helpers`
IMPORT `oa3-part1-residence`

-- Tests of oa3-part1-residence.l4 (regs 21 and 22). Every expected value is worked out by hand from the words of the
-- regulation; the dates are written with the dates beside them, and a "six months after" edge is tested on both sides.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Constructors the tests use (the encoding has no record update, so each is a rule with the varying facts as inputs).
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      g IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 21(2.1): Purpose for which a person is present in Canada`
`oa3test: purpose` a b c d e f g MEANS
    `reg 21(2.1): Purpose for which a person is present in Canada` WITH
        `carrying out his duties as a properly accredited diplomat, consular officer, representative or official` IS a
        `of a country other than Canada` IS b
        `of the United Nations or any of its agencies` IS c
        `of any intergovernmental organization in which Canada participates` IS d
        `as a member of a military force present in Canada for training or for any other purpose in connection with the defence or security interests of Canada or under any treaty or agreement between Canada and another country` IS e
        `as the spouse, common-law partner or dependant of a person referred to in paragraph (a) or (b), or the dependant of that person's spouse or common-law partner` IS f
        `as a member of the staff of or as a person otherwise accompanying a person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS g

GIVEN e IS A `reg 21(5)(a): Employer of a person employed out of Canada`
      abode IS A BOOLEAN
      estab IS A BOOLEAN
      ended IS A MAYBE DATE
      back IS A MAYBE DATE
      age IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 21(5)(a): Facts about employment out of Canada`
`oa3test: employment` e abode estab ended back age MEANS
    `reg 21(5)(a): Facts about employment out of Canada` WITH
        employer IS e
        `had in Canada a permanent place of abode to which he intended to return` IS abode
        `maintained in Canada a self-contained domestic establishment` IS estab
        `the day on which his employment out of Canada ended` IS ended
        `the day on which he returned to Canada` IS back
        `attained, while employed out of Canada, an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` IS age

GIVEN k IS A `reg 21(5)(b): Employment or engagement of a person out of Canada`
      ended IS A MAYBE DATE
      back IS A MAYBE DATE
      age IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 21(5)(b): Facts about employment or engagement out of Canada`
`oa3test: engagement` k ended back age MEANS
    `reg 21(5)(b): Facts about employment or engagement out of Canada` WITH
        kind IS k
        `the day on which his employment or engagement out of Canada ended` IS ended
        `the day on which he returned to Canada` IS back
        `attained, while employed or engaged out of Canada, an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` IS age

GIVEN s1 IS A BOOLEAN
      s2 IS A BOOLEAN
      back IS A MAYBE DATE
      sback IS A MAYBE DATE
      sdied IS A MAYBE DATE
      age IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 21(5)(c): Facts about accompanying a spouse or common-law partner`
`oa3test: accompanying` s1 s2 back sback sdied age MEANS
    `reg 21(5)(c): Facts about accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` WITH
        `accompanying their spouse or common-law partner who was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS s1
        `accompanying their spouse or common-law partner who was absent from Canada for the purpose of attending school or university` IS s2
        `the day on which the person returned to Canada` IS back
        `the day on which their spouse or common-law partner returned to Canada` IS sback
        `the day on which their spouse or common-law partner died while so absent from Canada` IS sdied
        `while so absent from Canada, attained an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` IS age

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 21(5)(d): Facts about awaiting transportation to Canada`
`oa3test: awaiting` a b c MEANS
    `reg 21(5)(d): Facts about awaiting transportation to Canada` WITH
        `awaiting transportation to Canada during or immediately after World War II` IS a
        `unable to return to Canada owing to the dislocation of transportation facilities` IS b
        `returned to Canada when transportation became available` IS c

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 21(5)(e): Facts about accompanying a spouse awaiting transportation to Canada`
`oa3test: accompanying a spouse awaiting` a b c MEANS
    `reg 21(5)(e): Facts about accompanying a spouse awaiting transportation to Canada` WITH
        `accompanying his spouse who was resident in Canada and awaiting transportation to Canada during or immediately after World War II` IS a
        `unable to return to Canada owing to the dislocation of transportation facilities` IS b
        `returned to Canada when transportation became available` IS c

GIVEN dep IS A BOOLEAN
      acc IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      back IS A MAYBE DATE
      oback IS A MAYBE DATE
      odied IS A MAYBE DATE
      age IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 21(5)(f): Facts about a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend`
`oa3test: dependent` dep acc other back oback odied age MEANS
    `reg 21(5)(f): Facts about a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` WITH
        `a dependent person` IS dep
        `accompanying and residing outside Canada with the person on whom he was dependent` IS acc
        `the person on whom he was dependent resided in Canada and was absent from Canada in a circumstance specified in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS other
        `the day on which the dependent person returned to Canada` IS back
        `the day on which the person on whom he was dependent returned to Canada` IS oback
        `the day on which the person on whom he was dependent died while so absent from Canada` IS odied
        `while so absent from Canada, attained an age at which he was eligible to be paid a pension under the Act` IS age

GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      earn IS A BOOLEAN
      pension IS A BOOLEAN
      family IS A BOOLEAN
      filed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 21(8): Facts about a calendar year`
`oa3test: year` year earn pension family filed MEANS
    `reg 21(8): Facts about a calendar year` WITH
        `calendar year` IS year
        `had unadjusted pensionable earnings above the basic exemption (Canada Pension Plan) or the personal exemption (Quebec Pension Plan) for that year` IS earn
        `received a retirement pension or disability pension under the Canada Pension Plan or An Act respecting the Québec Pension Plan` IS pension
        `had time excluded from a contributory period because a family allowance recipient, or time not included in a contributory period because a recipient of family benefits` IS family
        `filed an income tax return as a resident of Canada with the Minister of National Revenue` IS filed

-- k consecutive calendar years from `start`, every one with the same four facts.
GIVEN start IS A NUMBER
      k IS A NUMBER
      earn IS A BOOLEAN
      pension IS A BOOLEAN
      family IS A BOOLEAN
      filed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 21(8): Facts about a calendar year`
`oa3test: years` start k earn pension family filed MEANS
    IF k AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE `oa3test: year` start earn pension family filed FOLLOWED BY `oa3test: years` (start PLUS 1) (k MINUS 1) earn pension family filed

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(1)(a) and (b).
#ASSERT `reg 21(1)(a): the person resides in Canada` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(1)(a): the person resides in Canada` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(1)(a): the person resides in Canada` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(1)(a): the person resides in Canada` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(1)(b): the person is present in Canada` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(1)(b): the person is present in Canada` FALSE)

-- 21(2).
#ASSERT `reg 21(2): the person is deemed not to be living in any part of Canada` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(2): the person is deemed not to be living in any part of Canada` FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(2.1): a person who is not a citizen or permanent resident, present for one of four purposes.
-- purpose inputs: duties-as-diplomat, of another country, of the UN, of an intergovernmental organization, military, family, staff.
-- A citizen or permanent resident is never excluded, whatever the purpose.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` TRUE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Not present in Canada: nothing to exclude.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE FALSE (`oa3test: purpose` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (a)(i): duties for a country other than Canada.
#ASSERT `reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (a)(ii): duties for the United Nations or its agencies.
#ASSERT `reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (a)(iii): duties for an intergovernmental organization in which Canada participates.
#ASSERT `reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (a): duties as an accredited diplomat but for none of (i) to (iii): not within (a).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- One of (i) to (iii) without the duties: not within (a).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (b), (c) and (d).
#ASSERT `reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Present for none of the four purposes.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(2.1): the person does not reside in Canada during the period` FALSE TRUE (`oa3test: purpose` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(3)(a): returned before, or within six months after, the other's return or death.
-- Other returned 2020-01-01: six months after is 2020-07-01.
#ASSERT `reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (JUST (YMD 2020 7 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (JUST (YMD 2020 7 2)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING)
-- Before the other's return: counts ("either before or within six months after").
#ASSERT `reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (JUST (YMD 2019 12 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING
-- Other returned 2020-08-31: six months after clamps to 2021-02-28.
#ASSERT `reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (JUST (YMD 2021 2 28)) (JUST (YMD 2020 8 31)) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (JUST (YMD 2021 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 8 31)) NOTHING)
-- The other never returned but died while so absent on 2020-01-31: six months after is 2020-07-31.
#ASSERT `reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (JUST (YMD 2020 7 31)) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (JUST (YMD 2020 8 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)))
-- The person has not returned; or the other neither returned nor died.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(3)(a): the person returns to Canada before or within six months after the return of the other person, or within six months after that person's death` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING NOTHING)

-- 21(3) as a whole.
#ASSERT `reg 21(3): the period outside Canada is considered a period of residence and presence in Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 21(3): the period outside Canada is considered a period of residence and presence in Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(3): the period outside Canada is considered a period of residence and presence in Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(3): the period outside Canada is considered a period of residence and presence in Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(4): temporary and not more than one year, or school or university, or specified in (5).
-- Absence from 2020-01-01: one year after is 2021-01-01 (the anniversary day is within the year: fork F-21(4)).
#ASSERT `reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 12 31) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2021 1 1) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2021 1 2) FALSE FALSE)
-- Leap-day start: one year after 2020-02-29 clamps to 2021-02-28.
#ASSERT `reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 2 29) (YMD 2021 2 28) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 2 29) (YMD 2021 3 1) FALSE FALSE)
-- Short but not of a temporary nature: not within (a).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 2 1) FALSE FALSE)
-- (b): school or university, however long.
#ASSERT `reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2015 9 1) (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE FALSE
-- (c): specified in subsection (5), however long.
#ASSERT `reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 1 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) FALSE TRUE
-- None of the three.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 1 1) (YMD 2020 1 1) FALSE FALSE)
-- Not a person resident in Canada before the absence: nothing to interrupt.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(4): the interval of absence is deemed not to have interrupted the person's residence or presence in Canada` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2020 1 1) (YMD 2020 2 1) TRUE TRUE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(5)(a): employer (six), place of abode or establishment, and return within six months of the end or pension age.
-- Employment ended 2020-01-31: six months after is 2020-07-31.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(i): the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 7 31)) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(i): the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 8 1)) FALSE))
-- Late return, but pension age attained while so employed.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(i): the United Nations or one of its specialized agencies` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)) TRUE)
-- Establishment kept in Canada instead of an abode.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(iii): the Commonwealth Secretariat` FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) FALSE)
-- Neither abode nor establishment: fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(iii): the Commonwealth Secretariat` FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) TRUE))
-- Another employer: fails whatever else holds.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a): Another employer` TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) TRUE))
-- Employment not yet ended and not returned: only pension age can carry it.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(ii): the North Atlantic Treaty Organization` TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(ii): the North Atlantic Treaty Organization` TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING FALSE))
-- The other three listed employers.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(iv): the Organization of Economic Cooperation and Development` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(v): l'Agence de coopération culturelle et technique` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(a): the absence is in the circumstance of employment out of Canada` (`oa3test: employment` `reg 21(5)(a)(vi): a Canadian firm or corporation, as a representative or member thereof` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) FALSE)

-- 21(5)(b): nine kinds, the same return test, no place-of-abode condition.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(i): the Government of Canada or the government or a municipal corporation of any province` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 7 31)) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(i): the Government of Canada or the government or a municipal corporation of any province` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 8 1)) FALSE))
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(ii): the performance of services in another country under a development or assistance program sponsored or operated there by the Government of Canada or of a province or by a non-profit Canadian agency` NOTHING NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(iii): as a member of the Canadian Forces, pursuant to and in connection with the requirements of his duties` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(iv): work for Canada connected with the prosecution of any war` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(v): as a member of the armed forces of any ally of Canada during any war` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(vi): as a missionary with any religious group or organization` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(vii): as a worker in lumbering, harvesting, fishing or other seasonal employment` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(viii): as a transport worker on trains, aircraft, ships or buses running between Canada and points outside Canada or other similar employment` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b)(ix): as an employee, a member or an officer of an international charitable organization` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(b): the absence is in the circumstance of employment or engagement out of Canada` (`oa3test: engagement` `reg 21(5)(b): Another employment or engagement` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) TRUE))

-- 21(5)(c): accompanying a spouse or common-law partner; the spouse returned 2020-01-01 (six months after: 2020-07-01).
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(c): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` (`oa3test: accompanying` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 7 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(c): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` (`oa3test: accompanying` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 7 2)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING FALSE))
-- School or university instead of (a) or (b).
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(c): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` (`oa3test: accompanying` FALSE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING FALSE)
-- The spouse died while absent on 2020-01-31: six months after is 2020-07-31.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(c): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` (`oa3test: accompanying` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 7 31)) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(c): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` (`oa3test: accompanying` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 8 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) FALSE))
-- (ii): attained pension age while absent, whenever returned.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(c): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` (`oa3test: accompanying` TRUE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING TRUE)
-- Not accompanying a spouse absent for any listed purpose: fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(c): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse or common-law partner` (`oa3test: accompanying` FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING TRUE))

-- 21(5)(d) and (e): all three facts are needed.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(d): the absence is in the circumstance of awaiting transportation to Canada` (`oa3test: awaiting` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(d): the absence is in the circumstance of awaiting transportation to Canada` (`oa3test: awaiting` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(d): the absence is in the circumstance of awaiting transportation to Canada` (`oa3test: awaiting` TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(d): the absence is in the circumstance of awaiting transportation to Canada` (`oa3test: awaiting` TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(e): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse awaiting transportation to Canada` (`oa3test: accompanying a spouse awaiting` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(e): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse awaiting transportation to Canada` (`oa3test: accompanying a spouse awaiting` FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(e): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse awaiting transportation to Canada` (`oa3test: accompanying a spouse awaiting` TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(e): the absence is in the circumstance of accompanying a spouse awaiting transportation to Canada` (`oa3test: accompanying a spouse awaiting` TRUE TRUE FALSE))

-- 21(5)(f): a dependent person accompanying and residing with the person on whom dependent.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(f): the absence is in the circumstance of a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` (`oa3test: dependent` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 7 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(f): the absence is in the circumstance of a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` (`oa3test: dependent` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 7 2)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING FALSE))
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(f): the absence is in the circumstance of a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` (`oa3test: dependent` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (YMD 2020 7 31)) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 31)) FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5)(f): the absence is in the circumstance of a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` (`oa3test: dependent` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(f): the absence is in the circumstance of a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` (`oa3test: dependent` FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(f): the absence is in the circumstance of a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` (`oa3test: dependent` TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5)(f): the absence is in the circumstance of a dependent person accompanying the person on whom they depend` (`oa3test: dependent` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING TRUE))

-- 21(5) as a whole: any one of the six.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5): the absence is one of the absences specified in subsection (5)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 21(5): the absence is one of the absences specified in subsection (5)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 21(5): the absence is one of the absences specified in subsection (5)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 21(5): the absence is one of the absences specified in subsection (5)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 21(5): the absence is one of the absences specified in subsection (5)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 21(5): the absence is one of the absences specified in subsection (5)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5): the absence is one of the absences specified in subsection (5)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(5.1): all three conditions, and only for an allowance.
#ASSERT `reg 21(5.1): the absence is not considered to have interrupted the residence or presence in Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5.1): the absence is not considered to have interrupted the residence or presence in Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5.1): the absence is not considered to have interrupted the residence or presence in Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5.1): the absence is not considered to have interrupted the residence or presence in Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- 21(5.2) and (5.3).
#ASSERT `reg 21(5.2): the period of pensionable employment is considered a period of residence in Canada` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5.2): the period of pensionable employment is considered a period of residence in Canada` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5.2): the period of pensionable employment is considered a period of residence in Canada` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(5.3): the person is deemed not to be resident in Canada` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(5.3): the person is deemed not to be resident in Canada` FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(6) and (7): the ten relatives.
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the person's father`
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the person's mother`
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the person's brother`
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the person's sister`
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the person's child`
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the person's foster child`
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the father of the person's spouse or common-law partner`
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the mother of the person's spouse or common-law partner`
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the child of the person's spouse or common-law partner`
#ASSERT `reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): the foster child of the person's spouse or common-law partner`
-- Not a listed relative (a brother of the spouse is not listed).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` TRUE `reg 21(6): Another relative or no relative`)
-- The person was not absent in a (5)(a) or (b) circumstance: no dependent person.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(6): the relative is a dependent person for the purposes of paragraph (5)(f)` FALSE `reg 21(6): the person's father`)
-- (7): each of the three contexts, and none.
#ASSERT `reg 21(7): the relative is a dependant` TRUE FALSE FALSE `reg 21(6): the person's child`
#ASSERT `reg 21(7): the relative is a dependant` FALSE TRUE FALSE `reg 21(6): the father of the person's spouse or common-law partner`
#ASSERT `reg 21(7): the relative is a dependant` FALSE FALSE TRUE `reg 21(6): the person's foster child`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(7): the relative is a dependant` FALSE FALSE FALSE `reg 21(6): the person's child`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(7): the relative is a dependant` TRUE TRUE TRUE `reg 21(6): Another relative or no relative`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21(8)(a): forty years, each by one of the three limbs.
#ASSERT `reg 21(8)(a): the information indicates forty years` (`oa3test: years` 1965 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(8)(a): the information indicates forty years` (`oa3test: years` 1965 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Thirty-nine years of earnings plus one year of pension received: forty years by different limbs.
#ASSERT `reg 21(8)(a): the information indicates forty years` (append (`oa3test: years` 1965 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`oa3test: years` 2004 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- Thirty-nine by earnings, one by the family-allowance limb.
#ASSERT `reg 21(8)(a): the information indicates forty years` (append (`oa3test: years` 1965 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`oa3test: years` 2004 1 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- Forty years in which none of the three held: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(8)(a): the information indicates forty years` (`oa3test: years` 1965 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- Fifty years: yes.
#ASSERT `reg 21(8)(a): the information indicates forty years` (`oa3test: years` 1960 50 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- 21(8)(b): forty qualifying years, a return for the most recent year, and forty returns outside 1969 to 1971.
-- Forty-three qualifying years from 1966 (1966 to 2008), all with returns: 1969, 1970 and 1971 are not counted, so forty returns count.
#ASSERT `reg 21(8)(b): the information indicates forty years and returns filed` (`oa3test: years` 1966 43 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) TRUE
-- Forty-two: thirty-nine returns count, so no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(8)(b): the information indicates forty years and returns filed` (`oa3test: years` 1966 42 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) TRUE)
-- Forty qualifying years from 1960 (1960 to 1999): thirty-seven returns outside 1969 to 1971, so no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(8)(b): the information indicates forty years and returns filed` (`oa3test: years` 1960 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) TRUE)
-- Forty-five from 1966, but no return for the most recent calendar year: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(8)(b): the information indicates forty years and returns filed` (`oa3test: years` 1966 45 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) FALSE)
-- Forty-five qualifying years from 1980, returns filed for only thirty-nine of them: no. (39 returns, 6 not filed)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(8)(b): the information indicates forty years and returns filed` (append (`oa3test: years` 1980 39 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) (`oa3test: years` 2019 6 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) TRUE)
-- Forty returns among forty-five qualifying years: yes.
#ASSERT `reg 21(8)(b): the information indicates forty years and returns filed` (append (`oa3test: years` 1980 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) (`oa3test: years` 2020 5 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) TRUE

-- 21(8) as a whole: the pension-recipient branch ignores returns; the other requires them.
#ASSERT `reg 21(8): the prescribed information for subparagraph 3(1)(c)(iii) of the Act has been made available` TRUE (`oa3test: years` 1965 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21(8): the prescribed information for subparagraph 3(1)(c)(iii) of the Act has been made available` FALSE (`oa3test: years` 1965 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 21(8): the prescribed information for subparagraph 3(1)(c)(iii) of the Act has been made available` FALSE (`oa3test: years` 1966 43 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 21 as a whole: the deemed-not limbs override; the other limbs add.
-- Ordinary residence: (1)(a) only.
#ASSERT `reg 21: the person resides in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not resident by (1)(a) and nothing adds: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21: the person resides in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- An interval of absence deemed not to interrupt: resident although (1)(a) is false for the time abroad.
#ASSERT `reg 21: the person resides in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- A period considered a period of residence under (3) or (5.2).
#ASSERT `reg 21: the person resides in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- (2), (2.1) and (5.3) each override everything else.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21: the person resides in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21: the person resides in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21: the person resides in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Presence.
#ASSERT `reg 21: the person is present in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 21: the person is present in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 21: the person is present in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 21: the person is present in Canada for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 22(1): each of the three limbs, with the other facts false.
#ASSERT `reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (b): resident and absent, deemed not to have interrupted, lawfully in Canada just before: all three needed.
#ASSERT `reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- (c): not resident but deemed resident: both needed.
#ASSERT `reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Nothing at all.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(1): the person is legally resident in Canada` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- 22(2): both the address and the information.
#ASSERT `reg 22(2): the prescribed information for paragraph 4(1)(a) of the Act has been made available` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(2): the prescribed information for paragraph 4(1)(a) of the Act has been made available` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 22(2): the prescribed information for paragraph 4(1)(a) of the Act has been made available` FALSE TRUE)
